{"t": 128.123, "n": 113, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "Phase 2 is built, and its four rows (2.1 to 2.4) are marked ✓ 2026-11-26 in the plan. `test_registry.py` passes: 11 tests, run on one worker. `test_scaffold.py` passes too: 21 tests. `ruff check` on the three changed files passes. I didn't run `mypy` or the other verification commands.\n\n- **Tests, written first:** the two new tests in `test_registry.py` failed before any source change. Both failed on the register rung: the linked-worktree copy was refused as `name-taken`.\n- **`other_checkout`:** the new function in `package/registry.py` returns the registered path. It does so only when both folders share one git common dir and sit at the same place from their top levels. `register` is untouched, so `workflows register` still refuses.\n- **`_register`:** in `author/verify.py`, a `name-taken` on the check-only call now ends rung 7 as passed. The note is `registered from <path>; the entry is unchanged`, and nothing is written. Other refusals, and a `name-taken` with no matching checkout, keep their findings.\n- **`name-taken` still holds:** a package from another repository, and one from another folder of the same repository, both still fail rung 7 with `name-taken`.\n\nARTIFACT phase_note: Ran plugins/tempergraph/engine/tests/test_registry.py (11 passed, -n 0) and tests/test_scaffold.py (21 passed). Deviations: (1) the new tests use a scaffolded package (`scaffold` and `session` from test_scaffold) rather than `minimal_package`, because `minimal_package` fails rung 4 (generated tests) before rung 7. (2) They compare the bytes of `registry.json` and its entry instead of `hash_tree` of the whole home, because the CLI writes stats and index files into the home on every call, so a tree hash cannot stay equal. (3) The rung's `_name_of` helper in verify.py reads the name from tempergraph.json. No spec outside the plan's front matter was found false; SCF-B24/B25 already state this behaviour.", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "05ea5d9c-99fd-4c54-981f-2f3500da0dce"}
